  "causebase_summary": "Circobats Incorporated is presented on its website as an Adelaide-based circus school that offers classes and workshops for children and adults. The site lists a regular term timetable for 2026, April school holiday workshops and full-day holiday programs for varying age groups, and specific holiday program dates (for example 4–8 March with multiple daily session times). It names a venue, “Circobats Community Circus,” and displays an enrolment period (13–17 April) and a 2026 timetable notice. The organisation also publishes performance activity: a CircoBats Performance Troupe production titled ‘The Dreamer’ is listed with an Adelaide Fringe run (26 January–12 April). The website text states that classes cover circus skills such as tumbling, aerial, juggling and spinning and says the programs are open to all skill levels. The available evidence is drawn from the organisation’s public website; no financial reports or independent evaluations were provided in the supplied evidence.",
